  {
   "taskKey": "min-motion-constant@configs/task.yaml",
   "description": "**Question.** At what luminance is red as bright as green for the visual system's motion pathway, for this observer?\n\n**What the observer sees and does.** A [[param:patch_size_dva]] patch of square-wave stripes at [[param:spatial_freq_cpd]] around a white cross on a blue square. A red/green grating (T1), a light/dark grating of their yellow mixture a quarter cycle on (T2), the red/green grating half a cycle on (T3) and the mixture three quarters on (T4) repeat at [[param:cycle_hz]]. If red is lighter than green the stripes seem to drift with the steps, if darker against them. The observer presses LEFT, RIGHT or DOWN (no consistent motion).\n\n**Varied.** Red luminance ([[param:test_levels_cd_m2]]) against green at [[param:reference_cd_m2]], and the step direction (left or right), [[param:paradigm.n_per_condition]] times each.\n\n**Measured.** Percent left, right and neither per red luminance; the PSE where neither direction prevails; the width of the neither band.\n\n**Meaning and limits.** The PSE is this observer's luminance match for this stimulus on this display. Physical cd/m2 need a measured photometry file; with the example file the values are nominal and device-specific. It is not a colour-vision test.",
   "timeline": {
    "caption": "One trial. The cycle T1-T4 repeats until a key; only the key wait is event-dependent.",
    "phases": [
     {
      "id": "fixate",
      "label": "Fixation cross",
      "timing": {
       "kind": "parameter",
       "param": "fixation_duration"
      },
      "start_events": [
       "FIX_ON"
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "respond",
      "label": "Cycle runs; report",
      "timing": {
       "kind": "event",
       "until": "LEFT, RIGHT or DOWN",
       "max": {
        "param": "response_timeout"
       }
      },
      "start_events": [
       "RESPONSE_CUE"
      ],
      "end_events": [
       "RESPONSE"
      ]
     }
    ],
    "tracks": [
     {
      "label": "Fixation cross on blue square",
      "role": "stimulus",
      "from": "fixate",
      "to": "respond"
     },
     {
      "label": "T1 T2 T3 T4 repeating, 50 ms each",
      "role": "stimulus",
      "from": "respond",
      "to": "respond"
     },
     {
      "label": "Key: left / right / neither",
      "role": "response",
      "from": "respond",
      "to": "respond"
